# CODEOWNERS — gates which approvals satisfy the "Require review from
# Code Owners" branch ruleset on `main`.
#
# Anyone listed here may approve PRs against the patterns they own.
# Combined with the matching branch ruleset toggle, only their approvals
# count toward the merge requirement. Non-owners can still leave reviews
# and comments; their approvals simply do not unblock merge.
#
# See: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# This file previously listed three handles inherited from the upstream fork
# (@jonsaadfalcon, @ANarayan, @robbym-dev). None of them has access to
# github.com/carlitoetienne01-spec/Diapason, so with the ruleset enabled no
# pull request could ever be unblocked — the gate named reviewers who cannot
# review. It now names the account that actually owns the repository.
#
# To add more owners, append GitHub handles (`@username`) to the line below.
# Team slugs (`@org/team`) only work under an organisation; this repository
# lives on a personal account. To gate specific paths differently, add a
# more-specific pattern beneath it (later, more specific rules win).

* @carlitoetienne01-spec
